{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535503-pattern-bleeding","id":1535503,"title":"Pattern bleeding","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-12T23:37:43-07:00","id":1535503,"title":"Pattern bleeding","content":"Does it only affect life sphere?<br /> Is a permament effect on a life pattern (for example fear aura on a dog) suseptable to pattern bleeding?<br /> How does the equivalent work for other patterns?<br /> What other systems do you use to unwave permament effects that are clearly magical?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-13T09:38:31-07:00","id":1535514,"title":"","content":"Pattern bleed is for situations where the pattern itself is unacceptable to reality. That\u2019s why it usually only applies to some Life effects, because those are changing the actual pattern. Your suggested fear effect is not changing the Dog\u2019s pattern so no pattern bleed is involved.<br /> <br /> Unweaving and unbelief are still applicable, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-14T21:19:16-07:00","id":1535608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535503-pattern-bleeding?p=1535514#post1535514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pattern bleed is for situations where the pattern itself is unacceptable to reality. That\u2019s why it usually only applies to some Life effects, because those are changing the actual pattern. Your suggested fear effect is not changing the Dog\u2019s pattern so no pattern bleed is involved.<br /> <br /> Unweaving and unbelief are still applicable, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't affect just Life thou, although it is the most common source.<br /> <br /> If you use Mind to get some &quot;superpowers&quot; it could also cause Pattern Bleeding.<br /> <br /> The most obvious use would be to use Mind 1 to get Mental Attributes over the level 5. But that's not the only way. Other than that thou, I think this would come with &quot;ST fiat&quot;. Using Mind 1 to get a &quot;permanent&quot; effect that allows you to think about 10 different things at the same time (split/several minds) would also lead to Pattern Bleeding - in my opinion.<br /> <br /> There are possibly others. Turning oneself into a living Talisman would probably qualify (if the effects are obviously Vulgar). Maybe some other examples I haven't thought about too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-20T01:46:24-07:00","id":1535977,"title":"","content":"My general rule of thumb is anything that could be granted by the Enhancements background leads to pattern bleed, so Mind or Life based augmentations, and so even a single extra dot in an attribute is enough.<br /> <br /> bare in mind, have stats reduced does not lead to pattern bleed. Otherwise you get situations where you can curse someone with reduced stamina and then force them to pattern bleed to death, which is not the intent of this mechanic","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 05-20-2024, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T08:45:39-07:00","id":1536059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535503-pattern-bleeding#post1535503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What other systems do you use to unwave permament effects that are clearly magical?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, true permanency it's optional. The ST needs to determine if an effect can be made permanent. Otherwise the effect would last 6 moths as much before needing a re-cast. I've always tought sensible to limit permanency to things that could pass as normal if left alone (like how most Talismans look as relatively normal objects before activated).<br /> <br /> Arguably, unbelief could also terminate an effect before it's time, albeit that's not ruled anywhere AFAIK - but I think you could use it to justify houserules to that end<br /> <br /> EDIT: There's also Permanent Paradox. Not really unweaving anything, but much like &quot;pattern bleed&quot; it does make preserving a vulgar effect a pain in the ***.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-21-2024, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T13:41:51-07:00","id":1536080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535503-pattern-bleeding?p=1536059#post1536059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, true permanency it's optional. The ST needs to determine if an effect can be made permanent. Otherwise the effect would last 6 moths as much before needing a re-cast. I've always tought sensible to limit permanency to things that could pass as normal if left alone (like how most Talismans look as relatively normal objects before activated).<br /> <br /> Arguably, unbelief could also terminate an effect before it's time, albeit that's not ruled anywhere AFAIK - but I think you could use it to justify houserules to that end<br /> <br /> EDIT: There's also Permanent Paradox. Not really unweaving anything, but much like &quot;pattern bleed&quot; it does make preserving a vulgar effect a pain in the ***.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unbelief really only functions as a justification for ending effects early and making life difficult for bygones and the like. I think both are intentional, not house rules, even if there are not clear systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T10:46:46-07:00","id":1536263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535503-pattern-bleeding?p=1536059#post1536059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, true permanency it's optional. The ST needs to determine if an effect can be made permanent. Otherwise the effect would last 6 moths as much before needing a re-cast. I've always tought sensible to limit permanency to things that could pass as normal if left alone (like how most Talismans look as relatively normal objects before activated).<br /> <br /> Arguably, unbelief could also terminate an effect before it's time, albeit that's not ruled anywhere AFAIK - but I think you could use it to justify houserules to that end<br /> <br /> EDIT: There's also Permanent Paradox. Not really unweaving anything, but much like &quot;pattern bleed&quot; it does make preserving a vulgar effect a pain in the ***.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, i use the DA:MAGE system for permanence. That is, you need an obscene amount of successes as well as quintessence. <br /> Coincidentally, it makes quint a lot more useful as a resource but that's another matter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}